# Copy to .env. Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser,
# so never put a secret in here - everything below ships in the bundle.

# Where the Django API is mounted.
#
# Left unset on purpose. src/services/api.ts then points at port 8000 on
# whichever host the page was opened from, so the same build works at
# localhost and at the machine's LAN address when you open it on a phone.
# Setting it here pins every request to one host and breaks that - which is
# exactly what you want in production, and not in development.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com
